Title: Parallel Future Backend using 'mizu'
Description: Implementation of the Future API <doi:10.32614/RJ-2021-048> on
    top of the 'mizu' package <doi:10.32614/CRAN.package.mizu>. The backend
    is fully compliant with the Future API, as validated by the
    'future.tests' conformance test suite, meaning that code using futures
    gives identical results and behaves the same regardless of which future
    backend is used. Futures are resolved in parallel on the local machine
    by R worker processes that exchange data via shared memory. A common use
    is to parallelize existing map-reduce calls via the 'futurize' package
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2601.17578>, e.g.
    'plan(future.mizu::mizu_multisession)' followed by 'lapply(xs, fcn) |>
    futurize()' or 'purrr::map(xs, fcn) |> futurize()'.
